# PowerShell is delivered to Windows machines, where CRLF is the convention.
# Storing CRLF in the repository instead would make every line of the file look
# like trailing whitespace to `git diff --check`, because the \r is exactly
# that. Declaring the ending here keeps the repository copy LF, hands Windows a
# CRLF working copy, and leaves the whitespace check meaningful.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
